Documentation for mmig_decode
-----------------------------
rev 0.2, 05/11/00:   Fixed bug in call to mmig_AOn1
rev 0.1, 02/10/00:   Initial release


This generator is used to derive binary decoders.  The user selects
the number of input bits, the desired output drive size, a special
mode (if desired), and whether or not to bitslice the resulting
design.

The special modes are as follows:
  None      :  Decoder_Out = binary_decode(Decoder_In)

  Enable    :  if {enable == 1}
                  Decoder_Out = 0
               else
                  Decoder_Out = binary_decode(Decoder_In)

  ForceZero :  if {forcezero == 1}
                  Decoder_Out = 000...001
               else
                  Decoder_Out = binary_decode(Decoder_In)
        


GENERATOR ARGUMENTS:
--------------------
  NBITS:
    Definition: 
      The number of data inputs.
    Legal values:
      2 <= NINPUTS <= 128
    Default:
      4

  OutputSize:
    Definition:
      The desired output drive strength.
    Legal Values:
      B, C, D, E
    Default:
      B

  SpecialModes:
    Definition:
      Allows the user to select special features to be added to
      the binary decoder.  See discussion above.
    Legal Values:
      None, Enabled, ForceZero
    Default:
      None

  BitSlice:
    Definition:
      The user may choose to force the gates to be placed within one
      bit pitch (BitSlice = "Y") or to allow the gates to be placed
      within one row, in as many bit pitches as necessary (BitSlice = 
      "N").  The former is more useful for datapath applications, the
      latter is more useful for control sections.
    Legal Values:
      Y or N
    Default:
      N

